Stable ids move to scheme v17: one bump for every fix below that moves an id.

Fixes (each its own commit):
- Swift: argument labels and static vs instance members are hashed (overloads that differ only by label, or a static and an instance member of one name, no longer tie).
- Swift: local declarations are scoped by their enclosing callable.
- Dart: a named parameter's name is hashed (callers write it).
- Function-type parameter names are left out of hashed types (Go, Kotlin, Swift, TypeScript).
- JS/TS: static vs instance class members are hashed.
- Java: anonymous classes are scoped by binding, type and overload.
- Rust #[cfg] guards and Swift #if branches enter the id.
- A type name is hashed through the file's imports: the qualified and the imported spelling of one type get one id. Language-default names (java.lang, Kotlin/Scala defaults, Rust prelude) are written by their simple name.
- Guard fixes: lru_cache for chain patterns; the rust_scip parity test is marked incumbent_fed.

